## Context
Author ruling, 2026-10-27 raid. The raid's one-fix-round breaker (`skills/raid/references/fix-and-regate.md`:
"FINDINGS again on the fixes after the narrower gaze → ESCALATE") fired on PRs #1755 and #1756; both
second-round findings were real, local fixes to the first round's own fixes, and each cost the author an
interruption. Upstream cause: producers wrote tests after code or tests that never failed for the
targeted reason (PR #1756's first round; mutation testing found survivors).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A second fix round runs without the author when every finding of the narrower gaze is about the
      previous fixes (no new scope), is tagged `verifiable` with a reproduction, and the fix is
      red-test-first; a third round, or any judgment finding, escalates. Stated once (fix-and-regate.md),
      cited from /merge § Before merging.
- [ ] Hunt's Execute step requires the red run to be shown failing for the targeted reason (not an
      import or argument error), and the fix-round contract says the same.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

